      "writtenOn": "2025-08-18T21:11:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "just curious, why do we have rwx and rx only and not the rest?. Would it be better to have accessor functions which derives the needed mask from a single prot_mask rather than having individual fields for the mask that we need in the code?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 109,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 112,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "fixSuggestions": [
        {
          "fixId": "eb03adb1_deb96013",
          "description": "prompt_to_edit API",
          "replacements": [
            {
              "path": "arch/x86/kvm/pkvm/vmx/ept.c",
              "range": {
                "startLine": 110,
                "startChar": 0,
                "endLine": 110,
                "endChar": 0
              },
              "replacement": "\t/*\n\t * The prot_rwx is used to check if the page is writable.\n\t * The prot_rx is used to check if the page is readable and executable.\n\t */\n"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "revId": "403551799453aab94f91ad5a112e7045ef13733f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a76a457a_b178875c",
        "filename": "arch/x86/kvm/pkvm/vmx/ept.c",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 112,
      "author": {
        "id": 2022314
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-08-18T22:59:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e just curious, why do we have rwx and rx only and not the rest?\n\nBecause we don\u0027t have use cases for non-executable mappings so far (and KVM\u0027s uAPI doesn\u0027t support them). Although KVM internally uses non-executable huge pages, to work around a bug in older CPUs: https://docs.kernel.org/admin-guide/hw-vuln/multihit.html but that creates a plenty of extra complexity (dynamically splitting those pages into small executable pages when the guest wants to execute them, plus taking that into account in various corner cases), so I\u0027ve disabled that workaround for simplicity: aosp/3700491\n\n\u003e Would it be better to have accessor functions which derives the needed mask from a single prot_mask rather than having individual fields for the mask that we need in the code?\n\nThe reason for using these static masks is that we simply don\u0027t need to derive them at runtime every time, we can just set them once. (The memory type bits, for instance, are a bit different story. We do derive them at runtime using kvm_x86_call(get_mt_mask), as you can see in the next patches.)\n\nAlso KVM does that similarly, see e.g. kvm_mmu_set_ept_masks().\n\nThough I\u0027m not against doing this differently, if that makes it better in some way. Do you have some specific proposals?",
      "parentUuid": "c8d21004_efa263a6",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 109,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 112,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "403551799453aab94f91ad5a112e7045ef13733f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c1a21986_0194cf49",
        "filename": "arch/x86/kvm/pkvm/vmx/ept.c",
