      "writtenOn": "2025-08-19T14:02:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Because we don\u0027t have use cases for non-executable mappings so far (and KVM\u0027s uAPI doesn\u0027t support them). Although KVM internally uses non-executable huge pages, to work around a bug in older CPUs: https://docs.kernel.org/admin-guide/hw-vuln/multihit.html but that creates a plenty of extra complexity (dynamically splitting those pages into small executable pages when the guest wants to execute them, plus taking that into account in various corner cases), so I\u0027ve disabled that workaround for simplicity: aosp/3700491\n\nGot it, thanks\n\n\u003e The reason for using these static masks is that we simply don\u0027t need to derive them at runtime every time, we can just set them once. (The memory type bits, for instance, are a bit different story. We do derive them at runtime using kvm_x86_call(get_mt_mask), as you can see in the next patches.)\n\nyeah true, it makes sense to have it static as it doesn\u0027t change for a particular vendor.",
      "parentUuid": "a76a457a_b178875c",
