        "id": 3702829
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-08-19T14:02:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`kvm_mmu_set_ept_masks` is a bit different I guess - that is intel specific and I am not sure if the masks set in `kvm_mmu_set_ept_masks` are used for svm code. If I understand correctly, pkvm_ept_set_mmu_caps() is actually setting two global variables `guest_pgt_ops` and `guest_pgt_cap` that is supposed to be vendor agnostic and could be used in SVM as well. I was just trying to point out that the code is not fully vendor agnostic in this case.\n\nMy initial proposal was to have vendor agnostic function called from vendor_module_init that calls into vendor specific function. But now when I think about it, it doesn\u0027t give any advantage over calling `pkvm_npt_set_mmu_caps()` from svm_hardware_init and `pkvm_ept_set_mmu_caps()` from vmx_hardware_init. I am fine with this implementation. Rescinding my proposal :-)",
      "parentUuid": "aee7de2b_2a9a074a",
      "revId": "403551799453aab94f91ad5a112e7045ef13733f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "147275f9_47f8e85d",
        "filename": "arch/x86/kvm/pkvm/vmx/vmx.c",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 7654,
