      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-08-19T14:47:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`guest_pgt_ops` and `guest_pgt_cap` are set by vendor-specific code but used by vendor-agnostic code in vendor-agnostic way. Just like KVM\u0027s `shadow_user_mask`, `shadow_accessed_mask` etc which are set by `kvm_mmu_set_ept_masks()` on Intel, while on AMD they remain set to the default values in `kvm_mmu_reset_all_pte_masks()` (since, I guess, NPT, unlike EPT, has PTEs format compatible with regular, stage-1 page tables), but after that they are used by KVM MMU the same way on both Intel and AMD.",
      "parentUuid": "4aa44952_bc2dbae5",
      "revId": "403551799453aab94f91ad5a112e7045ef13733f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
