      "writtenOn": "2025-08-19T16:09:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah, I think I see your point. I was also hesitating as to whether it is a good idea to \"abuse\" `pkvm_pgtable_cap` by adding fields that are not used by pgtable.c. Now it seems cleaner to add a separate structure for them, e.g. `pkvm_pgtable_masks`, or for example just make them all global variables (again, similarly to KVM with its `shadow_user_mask`, `shadow_accessed_mask` etc).\n\nAlso slightly independently of that, I\u0027ve realized it\u0027s better to rename them to `perm_mask`, `perm_rwx` and `perm_rx`, to not confuse with \"prot\" used in `table_prot`, `pgt_entry_to_prot()` etc where it is used with a different meaning: it stands for \"protection\" but actually means not just the protection bits (rwx) but any bits beyond the address bits. (This naming style is kind of inherited from ARM, see `enum kvm_pgtable_prot`)",
      "parentUuid": "c39edc9b_fd2a5911",
